## Overview

Glial Core AI™ is a deterministic, sharded, supervisory runtime architecture designed around a **non-neuronal glial-style control model** rather than a purely execution-centric neuron-only model.

The operational environment is deployed through **AiSearchEngine.com**.

This repository exists to make the system publicly inspectable through:

- benchmark packs
- seeded reproducibility baselines
- fault-injection scenarios
- artifact schemas
- CI validation workflows
- deployment manifests
- public submission and review procedures

The repository is therefore not just source code. It is the **public evidence and validation layer** for the operational runtime.

---

## Boundary of Claim

This repository and its associated operational runtime support:

- deterministic bounded execution within a validated runtime envelope
- procedural targeting of an 85-billion logical registry
- sharded active-window execution
- supervisory verification of encoded integrity predicates
- checkpoint, rollback, and quiescence behavior
- public benchmark and fault-validation workflows

They do **not** by themselves establish:

- universal correctness of all outputs
- universal truth of all emitted propositions
- full simultaneous dense residency of all 85 billion nodes
- completed real-world efficacy across institutional or bio-robotic domains
- peer-reviewed confirmation of the underlying doctrine

